say what the main bundle was derived from

CFBundleGetMainBundle returning NULL says nothing about which of the four steps failed. With
CIDER_TRACE_MAINBUNDLE set it prints the process path, the executable URL and the bundle URL, and
that is what showed all three were derived correctly and _CFBundleCreate rejected the result
anyway: for a version 3 bundle it requires an existing DIRECTORY, and the path it is handed is the
HOST spelling, which does not exist inside the container.

The same probe on MoneyMoney prints /Applications/MoneyMoney.app, so an in-prefix application is
unaffected. Task #205.

